    description: "FOUND 2026-08-28 while relocating the haskell third-party rows for WI-surun (ADR-0047 ruling 1). Not fixed there on purpose: WI-surun changes WHERE a row lives, not what it claims, and mixing a boundary correction into a relocation would have made its A/B measure two things at once.\n\nTHE ROWS. haskell's Network.Wai block is catalogued net_recv:\n\n    Network.Wai.responseLBS       net_recv\n    Network.Wai.responseFile      net_recv\n    Network.Wai.responseBuilder   net_recv\n    Network.Wai.responseStream    net_recv\n\nThese are RESPONSE CONSTRUCTORS. They build the payload a server is about to\nsend. Building an outbound response is not receiving anything, and net_recv is\nan AUTO-DERIVED TAINT SOURCE via AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP -- so each of these\nMINTS untrusted_input at a call that observes nothing, which is the F5\nmechanism exactly.\n\nIT IS THE SAME DEFECT ALREADY FIXED IN ELIXIR, IN ANOTHER LANGUAGE. #609 moved\n26 Phoenix/Plug response helpers from net_recv to net_send for this reason, and\nrecorded the consequence: a Phoenix application had NO EGRESS SURFACE at all --\na false all-clear. The Wai rows are the Haskell spelling of the same thing, and\nthey were missed because that sweep was run per-catalogue rather than per-\nmechanism. LIVE.md rule 4: a named instance is usually the tip of a family;\nhere the family crosses languages.\n\nEXPECTED DIRECTION: net_recv -> net_send, matching #609. That both removes a\nfalse source AND restores an egress sink, so it is the rare correction that is\na pure win on both sides (contrast WI-lunav, where removing a sink deletes a\ncrossing nothing else represents).\n\nSEPARATE AND NOT CLAIMED HERE -- Network.Wai.Handler.Warp.run / runSettings /\nrunTLS / runEnv are also net_recv. Those are server LAUNCH calls, and the\nargument cuts both ways: the server genuinely receives, but the data reaches\nthe `app` handler rather than run's caller, so taint minted at the call site is\nattributed to a scope that never sees a request. That is the SAME question as\nPhoenix.Router, which #609 deliberately KEPT as a control. Adjudicate the two\ntogether and identically, or neither -- do not silently split them.\n\nMEASUREMENT: the f5_ab_ rig in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/ is directly reusable\nand already carries the NETWORK claims file this needs (the standing claims\nfile is host_fs-ONLY and would show nothing for a net_send change). postgrest\nis a confirmed-content Wai/Warp repo (Network.Wai in 50 files)."  # aac0
